  "slug": "stress-digital-twins-4fa2",
  "summary": "Patient-level and synthetic observables are now used to calibrate electrophysiology models at cell and tissue scales.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is parameterized in silico electrophysiology models tied to individual-level observables. Bayesian history matching personalises reaction-eikonal models of 17 hypertrophic cardiomyopathy patients from 252-electrode body surface potentials. A neural network trained on large synthetic electrophysiology datasets infers biophysical parameters and builds digital twins of excitable cells. A separate preprint models 117 transcriptomic-guided pediatric atrial cardiomyocyte populations and reports that age and heart rate jointly shape electrophysiology. Its calibration strategy is not described in the summary, so it contributes model-state heterogeneity rather than demonstrated fitting to patient data. What is new is the coupling of parameter inference to clinical or synthetic observables at cell and tissue scales.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-29"
}
